"""One switch for every on-table guidance cue in the benchmark.

The green placement discs and the green key-target ball exist for the human
operator: they say "put it here" / "press this one" during teleoperation. For a
policy they are a different thing entirely -- a marker that moves to the current
target broadcasts the active stage, so a model trained on frames containing it
can read the answer instead of solving the task.

Every one of these cues is visual only (no collision body) and none of them is
registered in the recorded environment state, so:

  * state-based training never sees them, with the switch either way;
  * image-based training sees them only if the RGB was rendered with them on,
    and this project renders RGB OFFLINE from recorded state -- so the same
    demonstrations can be re-rendered with cues for review and without them for
    training.

Before this existed each family spelled the toggle differently
(`show_charger_place_region`, `show_bolt_place_region`, `placement_region`,
`show_place_marker`, and office had none at all), so there was no way to ask a
re-render for "no cues" in one place. `show_guidance_markers=False` now turns
all of them off, and it composes with the per-subtask defaults rather than
replacing them: a stage that already hides its disc keeps hiding it.
"""

GUIDANCE_MARKER_KWARG = "show_guidance_markers"


def pop_guidance_marker_flag(kwargs: dict) -> bool:
    """Consume the flag from env kwargs.

    It has to be popped before ``BaseEnv.__init__`` sees it: ManiSkill rejects
    keyword arguments it does not know.
    """
    return bool(kwargs.pop(GUIDANCE_MARKER_KWARG, True))
